<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kakawin Bharatayuddha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1157</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kakawin Bharatayuddha is an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-javanese">Old Javanese</a> poem retelling the great war of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahabharata">Mahabharata</a>, completed in 1157 under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jayabaya">Jayabaya</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kediri-kingdom">Kediri</a>. It was begun by the poet Mpu Sedah and finished by Mpu Panuluh. It became one of the most influential works of Javanese literature and a source for the wayang shadow <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kakawin-bharatayuddha.jpg" alt="Kakawin Bharatayuddha" width="320" height="431" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gunning, Johannes Gerardus Hermanus, 1856-1914 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bharatayuddha-Gunning.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
